Return `201 Created` with an `ETag` and `Location` from `POST …/stages`,
in apps/api/docs/prototype/swagger.yaml

Generated on 2026-11-27, against the swagger.yaml committed in d6a23eb.
Apply from the repository root:

  git apply apps/api/docs/prototype/claude-exploration/api-patch-007-create-stage-etag.patch

Found while checking `data-sync-sequence.md` against swagger.yaml.
`PATCH` and `PUT` require `If-Match` with the Stage's current `ETag`
(`428` without it), but `POST …/stages` (`createStage`) returned no
`ETag`. A CMS would have had to `GET` every new Stage before its first
save. The user chose to fix the spec instead (User 2026-11-27):

1. `createStage` returns `201 Created`, not `200`, with an `ETag` header
   (the shared `ETag` header component) and a `Location` header giving
   the new Stage's URI. The description says to send the `ETag` as
   `If-Match` on the first `PATCH`.
2. The response body's `stage_id` is renamed `stageid`, matching the
   rest of the file.

